@lang en

-- us-ch1-construction.l4 : Title 1, chapter 1, sections 1 to 8 ("Rules of Construction").
-- Source: usc01.txt (plain-text rendering, not the official text). Quotation lines `-- src:N | ...` copy that file;
-- `python3 -I srcrefs.py check --strict <path to usc01.txt> us-ch1-construction.l4` checks them.
--
-- A definition that says a word "includes" things is not a closed list. Each function below is therefore named for what
-- the section EXPRESSLY includes, so that FALSE reads "section N does not say so", never "it is not so".
-- Where the section opens "unless the context indicates otherwise" (section 1), the context is an input, and a context
-- that indicates otherwise switches the section off.
--
-- Not encoded, with the reason of real length in NOTES.md: the canons of number, gender and tense (section 1, first
-- four limbs), the words "insane" and "insane person" (section 1), section 8(c) (a rule of non-construction).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `us-nouns`

§ `Chapter 1 - Rules of Construction`

§§ `Section 1 - Words denoting number, gender, and so forth`

-- INERT, section 1 limbs 1-4: the singular includes the plural and the plural the singular; the masculine includes the
-- feminine; the present tense includes the future. Canons about the form of words; the brief excuses them.
-- INERT, section 1 limb 5: "insane" and "insane person" include "every idiot, insane person, and person non compos mentis".
-- A list of archaic words for one another, with no test a program applies to facts about a person.

-- src:18 | In determining the meaning of any Act of Congress, unless the context indicates otherwise—
-- src:24 | the words “person” and “whoever” include corporations, companies, associations, firms, partnerships, societies, and joint stock companies, as well as individuals;
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 1, the words "person" and "whoever" (src:18 src:24)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of body`
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1 expressly includes the body in the words person and whoever` kind `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the context indicates otherwise`                   THEN FALSE
           IF kind EQUALS `a body of some other kind`             THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE TRUE

-- src:18 | In determining the meaning of any Act of Congress, unless the context indicates otherwise—
-- src:25 | “officer” includes any person authorized by law to perform the duties of the office;
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 1, the word "officer" (src:18 src:25)
GIVEN `the individual is authorized by law to perform the duties of the office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1 expressly includes the individual in the word officer` `the individual is authorized by law to perform the duties of the office` `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
        NOT `the context indicates otherwise`
    AND `the individual is authorized by law to perform the duties of the office`

-- src:18 | In determining the meaning of any Act of Congress, unless the context indicates otherwise—
-- src:26 | “signature” or “subscription” includes a mark when the person making the same intended it as such;
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 1, the words "signature" and "subscription" (src:18 src:26)
GIVEN `the person making the mark intended it as a signature or subscription` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1 expressly includes the mark in the words signature and subscription` `the person making the mark intended it as a signature or subscription` `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
        NOT `the context indicates otherwise`
    AND `the person making the mark intended it as a signature or subscription`

-- src:18 | In determining the meaning of any Act of Congress, unless the context indicates otherwise—
-- src:27 | “oath” includes affirmation, and “sworn” includes affirmed;
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 1, the words "oath" and "sworn" (src:18 src:27)
GIVEN `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1 treats an affirmation as an oath and an affirmed statement as sworn` `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    NOT `the context indicates otherwise`

-- src:18 | In determining the meaning of any Act of Congress, unless the context indicates otherwise—
-- src:28 | “writing” includes printing and typewriting and reproductions of visual symbols by photographing, multigraphing, mimeographing, manifolding, or otherwise.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 1, the word "writing" (src:18 src:28)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of reproducing a writing`
      `the context indicates otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1 expressly includes the way in the word writing` way `the context indicates otherwise` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the context indicates otherwise`                                  THEN FALSE
           IF way EQUALS `a way that does not reproduce visual symbols`          THEN FALSE
           OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Section 2 - "County" as including "parish", and so forth`

-- src:32 | The word “county” includes a parish, or any other equivalent subdivision of a State or Territory of the United States.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 2 (src:32)
GIVEN sub IS A `A subdivision`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 2 expressly includes the subdivision in the word county` sub MEANS
        sub's `it is a subdivision of a State or Territory of the United States`
    AND (   sub's `it is a parish`
         OR sub's `it is another equivalent subdivision`)

§§ `Section 3 - "Vessel" as including all means of water transportation`

-- src:36 | The word “vessel” includes every description of watercraft or other artificial contrivance used, or capable of being used, as a means of transportation on water.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 3 (src:36)
GIVEN thing IS A `A watercraft or other contrivance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 3 expressly includes the contrivance in the word vessel` thing MEANS
        (   thing's `it is a watercraft`
         OR thing's `it is another artificial contrivance`)
    AND (   thing's `it is used as a means of transportation on water`
         OR thing's `it is capable of being used as a means of transportation on water`)

§§ `Section 4 - "Vehicle" as including all means of land transportation`

-- src:40 | The word “vehicle” includes every description of carriage or other artificial contrivance used, or capable of being used, as a means of transportation on land.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 4 (src:40)
GIVEN thing IS A `A carriage or other contrivance`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 4 expressly includes the contrivance in the word vehicle` thing MEANS
        (   thing's `it is a carriage`
         OR thing's `it is another artificial contrivance`)
    AND (   thing's `it is used as a means of transportation on land`
         OR thing's `it is capable of being used as a means of transportation on land`)

§§ `Section 5 - "Company" or "association" as including successors and assigns`

-- src:44 | The word “company” or “association”, when used in reference to a corporation, shall be deemed to embrace the words “successors and assigns of such company or association”, in like manner as if these last-named words, or words of similar import, were expressed.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 5 (src:44)
GIVEN `the word is used in reference to a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 5 deems the words company and association to embrace successors and assigns` `the word is used in reference to a corporation` MEANS
    `the word is used in reference to a corporation`

§§ `Section 6 - Limitation of term "products of American fisheries"`

-- "fresh or frozen slices of fish substantially free of bone": the words "substantially free of bone" follow "of fish", so they are read
-- to qualify the slices only, and a fillet or a steak is within the exclusion whether or not it has bone (fork F-6; reading (ii) makes
-- the bone test govern all three). "(including any of the foregoing divided into sections)" adds no field: a divided fillet is a fillet.
-- src:48 | Wherever, in the statutes of the United States or in the rulings, regulations, or interpretations of various administrative bureaus and agencies of the United States there appears or may appear the term “products of American fisheries” said term shall not include fresh or frozen fish fillets, fresh or frozen fish steaks, or fresh or frozen slices of fish substantially free of bone (including any of the foregoing divided into sections), produced in a foreign country or its territorial waters, in whole or in part with the use of the labor of persons who are not residents of the United States.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 6 (src:48)
GIVEN product IS A `A fish product`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 6 excludes the product from the term products of American fisheries` product MEANS
        (   product's `it is a fresh or frozen fish fillet`
         OR product's `it is a fresh or frozen fish steak`
         OR (   product's `it is a fresh or frozen slice of fish`
             AND product's `it is substantially free of bone`))
    AND product's `it was produced in a foreign country or its territorial waters`
    AND product's `some of the labor used to produce it was that of persons who are not residents of the United States`

§§ `Section 7 - Marriage`

-- src:53 | (b) In this section, the term “State” means a State, the District of Columbia, the Commonwealth of Puerto Rico, or any other territory or possession of the United States.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 7(b) (src:53)
GIVEN place IS A `A place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 7(b) says the place is a State` place MEANS
    NOT (place EQUALS `a place outside any State`)

-- "shall be considered married IF": a sufficient condition. Section 7(a) does not say when an individual is NOT
-- considered married, so FALSE below reads "section 7(a) does not require it", not "unmarried" (fork F-7a in NOTES.md).
-- Section 7(c): only the law applicable when the marriage was entered into may be considered, which is the content of
-- the field `it is valid under the law applicable when it was entered into`.
-- src:52 | (a) For the purposes of any Federal law, rule, or regulation in which marital status is a factor, an individual shall be considered married if that individual’s marriage is between 2 individuals and is valid in the State where the marriage was entered into or, in the case of a marriage entered into outside any State, if the marriage is between 2 individuals and is valid in the place where entered into and the marriage could have been entered into in a State.
-- src:54 | (c) For purposes of subsection (a), in determining whether a marriage is valid in a State or the place where entered into, if outside of any State, only the law of the jurisdiction applicable at the time the marriage was entered into may be considered.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 7(a) and (c) (src:52 src:54)
GIVEN marriage IS A `A marriage`
      `marital status is a factor in the Federal law, rule or regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 7(a) considers the individual married` marriage `marital status is a factor in the Federal law, rule or regulation` MEANS
        `marital status is a factor in the Federal law, rule or regulation`
    AND marriage's `the number of individuals who are parties to it` EQUALS 2
    AND marriage's `it is valid under the law applicable when it was entered into`
    AND (   `section 7(b) says the place is a State` (marriage's `where it was entered into`)
         OR marriage's `it could have been entered into in a State`)

§§ `Section 8 - "Person", "human being", "child", and "individual" as including born-alive infant`

-- "regardless of whether the umbilical cord has been cut, and regardless of whether the expulsion or extraction occurs as
-- a result of natural or induced labor, cesarean section, or induced abortion": those two facts are in the record and
-- are read by nothing. "at any stage of development": no gestational field exists to be read.
-- src:59 | (b) As used in this section, the term “born alive”, with respect to a member of the species homo sapiens, means the complete expulsion or extraction from his or her mother of that member, at any stage of development, who after such expulsion or extraction breathes or has a beating heart, pulsation of the umbilical cord, or definite movement of voluntary muscles, regardless of whether the umbilical cord has been cut, and regardless of whether the expulsion or extraction occurs as a result of natural or induced labor, cesarean section, or induced abortion.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 8(b) (src:59)
GIVEN birth IS A `A birth`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 8(b) says the infant was born alive` birth MEANS
        birth's `there was complete expulsion or extraction from the mother`
    AND (   birth's `afterwards it breathes`
         OR birth's `afterwards it has a beating heart`
         OR birth's `afterwards it has pulsation of the umbilical cord`
         OR birth's `afterwards it has definite movement of voluntary muscles`)

-- Section 8(c) is a rule of non-construction ("Nothing in this section shall be construed to affirm, deny, expand,
-- or contract any legal status ... prior to being born alive"). So for a member that was not born alive, section 8(a)
-- affirms nothing and denies nothing, and FALSE below reads "section 8(a) does not include it".
-- src:58 | (a) In determining the meaning of any Act of Congress, or of any ruling, regulation, or interpretation of the various administrative bureaus and agencies of the United States, the words “person”, “human being”, “child”, and “individual”, shall include every infant member of the species homo sapiens who is born alive at any stage of development.
@ref 1 U.S.C. s 8(a) (src:58)
GIVEN birth IS A `A birth`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 8(a) includes the infant in the words person, human being, child and individual` birth MEANS
    `section 8(b) says the infant was born alive` birth
